# A Luxel library scene — Apache-2.0. Grammar: library/README.md.
# A mask can sit over pictures, not just patterns: a radar sweep pivots on the
# lighthouse lamp at the centre of a 32x32 harbour picture and reveals it, the
# phosphor's slow decay letting the coast sink back into the night. The ramp
# on the mask is a contrast curve — a floor of 20 % keeps the harbour faintly
# moonlit, and anything past mid-grey opens it fully.
S - Lighthouse
U 32 32
L color 0 0 0 0 normal 100 none fill 1
N Sea
K 0a1a2e
L sprite 0 0 0 0 normal 100 none fill 1
N Harbor
I @spr/harbor
L pat 0 0 0 0 mask 100 none fill 1
N Beam
I @pat/radar-2d
C sliderSweepSeconds 327680
C sliderPersistenceSeconds 163840
C sliderContacts 0
R 100 0:1c1c1c 100:ffffff
